<GuideLayout
  title="Planning multi day hikes in NSW"
  seoTitle="Multi Day Hikes in NSW: Overnight Walks and How to Book"
  pageImage={guideImage}
  pageImageAlt="Sandstone cliffs on the Coast Track, Royal National Park"
  description="Planning multi-day hikes in NSW? Beginner-friendly overnight walks near Sydney, harder routes to work up to, how campsite booking works and simple fire rules."
  eyebrow="Where to go"
  readTime="9 min read"
>
  <p>
    New South Wales has plenty of overnight walks, from easy two-day sections
    of the Great North Walk a train ride from Sydney to a tough hut-to-hut
    route on the mid-north coast. The hard part is not finding a track. It is
    picking one that suits your fitness and gear, and sorting out the booking
    and fire rules before you leave.
  </p>
  <p>
    This guide is aimed at first and second overnighters with a simple,
    budget kit. We point out which routes suit beginners and which ones to save
    for later, and link to a page for each so you can check current
    conditions.
  </p>

  <div class="takeaways">
    <strong>Key takeaways</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>
        For a first overnighter, try Wondabyne to Patonga or Berowra to Cowan
        on the Great North Walk. Both start and finish near public transport.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Royal National Park Coast Track is currently a day walk: its only
        campground, North Era, has been closed since July 2023.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Green Gully Track is for experienced hikers only, and the Main
        Range needs warm gear even in summer.
      </li>
      <li>Most NSW campsites, including free ones, need an online booking.</li>
      <li>Always tell someone your route and when you expect to be back.</li>
      <li>
        Blue Mountains routes are covered separately in our <a
          href="/guides/overnight-hikes-blue-mountains/"
          >overnight hikes Blue Mountains guide</a
        >; this guide covers the rest of the state.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your <a href="/guides/overnight-hike-packing-list/"
          >overnight hike packing list</a
        > and sleep system matter as much as the track you pick.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

